---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | GutCare Clinics"
  description="Read the GutCare Clinics Privacy Policy to understand how we collect, use, protect and manage your personal information."
>
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-50 via-white to-leaf-50/60 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="container-x">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold leading-[1.12] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Privacy <span class="highlight">Policy</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-10 sm:py-14">
    <article class="wp-content container-x">
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>Welcome to GutCare Clinics (<a href="https://www.gutcareclinics.com/">https://www.gutcareclinics.com/</a>).</p>
      <p>
        At GutCare Clinics, we respect your privacy and are committed to protecting the personal information you share
        with us through our website, appointment enquiry forms and other communication channels.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use and protect it, when we may share it, and
        the choices available to you when using our website.
      </p>
      <p>By accessing or using our website, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect personal information when you visit our website, contact us or submit an appointment enquiry.</p>

      <h3>A. Personal Information</h3>
      <p>The information we may collect includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full name</li>
        <li>Mobile number</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Appointment-related information</li>
        <li>Enquiry or communication details</li>
        <li>Any additional information you voluntarily provide.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>B. Health-Related Information</h3>
      <p>
        If you voluntarily share medical or health-related information while communicating with our clinic, we may
        collect and process that information to understand your enquiry and facilitate appropriate communication
        regarding healthcare services.
      </p>
      <p>Such information may include symptoms, medical history, treatment enquiries or other health-related details.</p>
      <p>
        We handle health-related information with appropriate care and confidentiality, subject to applicable legal
        requirements.
      </p>

      <h3>C. Automatically Collected Information</h3>
      <p>When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address</li>
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Device information</li>
        <li>Operating system</li>
        <li>Pages visited</li>
        <li>Date and time of website visits</li>
        <li>Referring website or traffic source.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>GutCare Clinics may use the collected information for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to appointment requests and enquiries.</li>
        <li>To contact patients regarding consultations and healthcare services.</li>
        <li>To provide information about treatments and clinic services.</li>
        <li>To coordinate appointment-related communication.</li>
        <li>To improve website functionality and user experience.</li>
        <li>To monitor website performance and visitor activity.</li>
        <li>To maintain website security and prevent spam or fraudulent activities.</li>
        <li>To comply with applicable legal and regulatory requirements.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We will process personal information only for legitimate and disclosed purposes, subject to applicable law and
        consent requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Appointment Enquiries and Communication</h2>
      <p>Our website allows visitors to submit appointment enquiries by providing their name and mobile number.</p>
      <p>When you submit an enquiry:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your submitted information may be used to contact you regarding your appointment request.</li>
        <li>Our authorised clinic representatives may access the information to respond to your enquiry.</li>
        <li>
          Your contact information may be retained as necessary for communication, record-keeping and applicable legal
          requirements.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Submitting an appointment enquiry through our website does not automatically confirm a medical appointment.</p>

      <h2>5. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may use cookies and similar tracking technologies to improve website performance and visitor
        experience.
      </p>
      <p>Cookies may be used to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Understand visitor behaviour and website traffic.</li>
        <li>Analyse website performance.</li>
        <li>Improve website navigation and functionality.</li>
        <li>Remember certain user preferences.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings.</p>
      <p>
        Where required by applicable law, we will obtain consent before placing non-essential cookies or using similar
        tracking technologies.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Google Analytics and Other Third-Party Tools</h2>
      <p>
        We may use third-party analytics and website performance tools, such as Google Analytics, to understand how
        visitors interact with our website.
      </p>
      <p>These tools may collect information such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Pages visited</li>
        <li>Session duration</li>
        <li>Browser and device information</li>
        <li>General website usage patterns</li>
        <li>Traffic sources.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The information collected through these services may be processed according to the respective third-party
        privacy policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        For more information about Google's privacy practices, visit:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </p>

      <h2>7. Sharing of Personal Information</h2>
      <p>GutCare Clinics does not sell personal information to third parties.</p>
      <p>However, we may share information in the following circumstances:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorised Clinic Personnel:</strong> With authorised staff who need the information to respond to
          enquiries or coordinate healthcare services.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Service Providers:</strong> With trusted website hosting, maintenance, security, analytics and
          communication service providers when necessary.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Healthcare Professionals:</strong> Where appropriate and necessary for healthcare-related services,
          subject to applicable confidentiality and legal requirements.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal Authorities:</strong> When disclosure is required under applicable laws, regulations, court
          orders or lawful government requests.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to ensure that third parties handling personal information maintain appropriate
        safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Data Security and Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorised
        access, disclosure, alteration, loss or misuse.
      </p>
      <p>These measures may include access controls, security monitoring and appropriate website protection practices.</p>
      <p>
        However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is completely secure. Therefore, we cannot guarantee
        absolute security of information transmitted over the internet.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was
        collected, including responding to enquiries, coordinating appointments, maintaining relevant records and
        meeting legal or regulatory obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Medical records, where applicable, may be retained separately in accordance with relevant healthcare
        record-retention requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        When information is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to securely delete or dispose of it,
        subject to applicable legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable data protection laws, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to personal information held about you.</li>
        <li>Request correction or updating of inaccurate information.</li>
        <li>Request deletion of personal information where legally permitted.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
        <li>Raise concerns regarding the use of your personal information.</li>
        <li>Submit a privacy-related grievance through the contact details provided below.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will review and respond to requests in accordance with applicable legal requirements.</p>

      <h2>11. External Website Links</h2>
      <p>Our website may contain links to third-party websites, social media platforms or external resources.</p>
      <p>These websites operate independently and may have their own privacy policies and data collection practices.</p>
      <p>
        GutCare Clinics is not responsible for the privacy practices, content or security of external websites. We
        encourage visitors to review the relevant privacy policies before sharing personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our website and healthcare services may be accessed by individuals seeking information about healthcare for
        themselves or their dependants.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where personal information relating to children is collected, we will handle it in accordance with applicable
        laws and obtain verifiable parental or guardian consent where required.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        GutCare Clinics reserves the right to update or modify this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes
        in our website, services, technology or applicable legal requirements.
      </p>
      <p>Any updates will be published on this page along with the revised Last Updated date.</p>
      <p>Visitors are encouraged to review this page periodically.</p>

      <h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions, concerns or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal
        information, please contact us:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>GutCare Clinics</strong><br />
        <strong>Address:</strong> 1st Floor, #4024, 13th 'H' Main, 1st Cross, HAL 2nd Stage, Indiranagar, Bengaluru,
        Karnataka – 560008, India.<br />
        <strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
        <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={site.phoneHref}>+91 8431550550</a><br />
        <strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.gutcareclinics.com/">https://www.gutcareclinics.com/</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        We will make reasonable efforts to address privacy-related enquiries and grievances in accordance with
        applicable laws.
      </p>

      <hr />
      <p>By using our website, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
